linux-system-hardener (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * RHEL 10 compliance profiles with report-time identifier translation.
  * New frameworks: SOC 2, NIST 800-171 r3, FedRAMP Moderate (10 total).
  * Scan performance: concurrent plugin execution; scan --timings flag.
  * Fix: services probe false PASS on CIS 2.2.3/2.2.4.
  * Fix: apply failure and fabricated change on hosts without a MAC system;
    no-op applies now report as skips (ChangeType::Skipped).
  * Per-command Tauri ACLs; Docker image; build identity in --version.
  * Docs and scripts restructured; packaging inputs moved under packaging/.

 -- Eric Jingryd <tidynest@proton.me>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0000

linux-system-hardener (1.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: checkpoint rollback could delete 0000-permission files (e.g. /etc/shadow).
  * Fix: permissions apply/rollback aborted when account-database paths were not allow-listed.
  * Security: accept RUSTSEC-2026-0097 (rand unsound; build-time transitive).

 -- Eric Jingryd <tidynest@proton.me>  Thu, 02 Jul 2026 06:30:00 +0000

